# Copy to .env and fill in before building a release.
#
# None of these values are secrets. Firebase's web config ships in the
# JavaScript bundle by design — it identifies the project, it does not grant
# access. The reCAPTCHA *site* key is public for the same structural reason:
# reCAPTCHA cannot run without it being in the page. What decides who may
# write what is App Check plus firestore.rules. See "Bảo mật" in README.md.
#
# Because they are not secrets, CI passes them as repository *variables*, not
# repository secrets. The only real secret is FIREBASE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT, which
# never reaches a browser.
#
# `npm run dev` needs none of this: it talks to the local Firestore emulator,
# which ignores App Check.
# Values come from Firebase console -> Project settings -> Your apps -> Web.

VITE_FIREBASE_API_KEY=AIzaSyXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX
VITE_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=your-project

# Only the admin dashboard at /ir-form/dashboard/ needs this one: the Google
# sign-in popup opens https://<authDomain>/__/auth/handler, so without it the
# first click goes nowhere. The student form never touches Auth — which is
# exactly why this value was missing until the dashboard came back.
#
# Firebase console -> Project settings -> Your apps -> Web, same block as the
# rest. Also add ump.ngthinh.com under Authentication -> Settings ->
# Authorized domains, or the popup is rejected on the real domain.
VITE_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=your-project.firebaseapp.com
VITE_FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET=your-project.firebasestorage.app
VITE_FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID=000000000000
VITE_FIREBASE_APP_ID=1:000000000000:web:xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# reCAPTCHA *Enterprise* site key (the key ID), from Firebase console ->
# App Check -> your web app. Enterprise keys have no secret key at all — that
# is a reCAPTCHA v3 concept. Nothing else about App Check belongs in this repo.
#
# The provider in src/lib/firebase.ts must match the key type registered in
# the console (ReCaptchaEnterpriseProvider here). A mismatch only shows up
# after enforcement is switched on, as permission-denied on every submission.
#
# Missing it in a release build means every submission is rejected once App
# Check enforcement is on, so `isConfigured` in src/lib/firebase.ts refuses to
# start without it.
VITE_RECAPTCHA_SITE_KEY=6LxXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX
